BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (the policy's out-of-network section, because where the EOB and the bill disagree 'is where the money lives') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm ([OWN7CBskcIQ @ 00:04:06]. Each disputed line gets a written, plain-words reason.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (Once errors are logged, the escalation ladder runs on scripts. Satra Taylor of Share My Lesson hands over the insurer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (line verbatim, 'Hi, I believe this bill is prohibited under the No Surprises Act. Can you confirm whether this was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (processed as an in network?', then tells collectors, 'This bill appears to violate the No Surprises Act. Please stop) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (collection and reprocess through my insurance company as an in-network claim' [Q11eG-8d-Hw @ 00:04:22]. Bill) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (Fighter says that single reprocessing call often solves the problem, and when it does not, the federal complaint at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (1-800-985-3059 is free, with providers facing fines up to $10,000 per violation, so hospitals that hear from CMS tend) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (to fix things quickly [1VtIU2oIxEY @ 00:06:28]. Evolutio Labs layers in the appeal content: name the No Surprises) Tj ET
