BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (The baseline mechanics are simple and unforgiving. Each side submits a single dollar figure, and the arbitrator picks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (one with no splitting. The insurer is then supposed to pay within 30 days, and balance billing the patient stays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (prohibited [nJ5Tz7G_LA8 @ 00:02:32]. Attorney Andrew Bethel lays out the front end. There is a 30-business-day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (open negotiation period. Multiple items, such as anesthesiology plus radiology, can be batched into one dispute. Notice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (goes to the federal portal the same day it goes to the other party. He also warns that only 39% of submitted disputes had) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (been resolved, leaving roughly 300,000 open [q3heX6QnFfo @ 00:04:42]. Gaines prices the administrative fee at $115) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (per dispute [QITUqT322Iw @ 00:38:30]. The About The Rest panel adds the real cost: 'you might get $50 a unit as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (QPA initially, but then you have to spend $1,000 per dispute to the IDRE.' Payment takes 9-12 months. Some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (companies win only 50-60% and lose money. Only about half of states use the federal process. The average award) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (lands around 2.3x QPA, or ask 150, get 100 [WdSfoeegaaI @ 00:20:29]. Every won dispute therefore carries a filing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (fee, a months-long lag and a collection risk before it ever becomes cash.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (The pricing fight is where the multiples get won. Gaines teaches the sharpest tactic: pull transparency allowed-amount) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (data by plan, zip, CPT and TIN to argue market rates. His example is 250% of Medicare in the market versus the 120%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (a plan actually paid. 'I can look up any TIN in the country and know exactly what they're getting paid,' he says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm ([QITUqT322Iw @ 00:41:15]. Velicky attacks the benchmark itself. The QPA rests on 2019 rates plus inflation, TMA 3) Tj ET
