BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 356.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.77 Tm (The costliest failures arrive after the money lands. The AR Specialist case shows Quantum Health and UMR) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.55 Tm (retroactively voiding single case agreements they had already approved, citing in-network facilities within 50 miles. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.32 Tm ($1,048.25 payment made on October 7 was reprocessed on November 4 and pulled back into recoupment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.10 Tm ([OLFRzRe0L2A @ 00:02:52]. The fix is to prove you are the only provider in the radius by calling competing facilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.87 Tm (yourself, then request the gap exception up front. The clock is brutal: exactly 180 days from the day-zero EOB to file) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.65 Tm (an out-of-network appeal, against 365 days in-network. Force reports a Cigna client facing a clawback in the millions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.42 Tm (for failing to send cost-share letters, the fee-forgiveness audit exposure Patriot Group flags directly [dUdxVBDLf5w @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.20 Tm (00:11:30]. Force also caught insurers calling a plan 110 percent of Medicare when the plan was actually UCR, which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.97 Tm (why the Patriot team pulls the SPD from the employer rather than trusting the carrier [dUdxVBDLf5w @ 00:07:33].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.75 Tm (Singh adds that signed settlement offers are not binding on the payer, so a closed deal can still be reopened, and tells) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.52 Tm (operators to fight recoupments rather than absorb them [7h4H8g1S01E @ 00:22:53].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 166.30 Tm (The second trap is reading an EOB at face value. Liz Taylor of MediGain walked through a UHC EOB where the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.07 Tm (allowed column showed $12,677 against $23,750 billed. The true allowance is billed minus the group-RC amount, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.85 Tm (anything not allowed at 100 percent without a stated methodology gets appealed [w387XkK0lkk @ 00:13:57]. Ellison) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 120.62 Tm (flags a newer payer move, double silent-PPO layering that tops allowables out closer to 30 and 40 percent, caught only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 105.40 Tm (by auditing EOBs [Pqx2hpp_cLU @ 00:18:50]. Singh's silent-PPO math shows how contracts keyed to allowed rather) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.17 Tm (than billed charges bleed value: $10,000 billed, $6,000 allowed, times 70 percent yields $4,200, and the payer picks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 74.95 Tm (whichever of contract or policy rate is lower [7h4H8g1S01E @ 00:33:05]. Behavioral Billing's dramatized case shows) Tj ET
