BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.77 Tm (Title: Small superbill moves that keep reimbursement flowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 501.55 Tm (Body: Field-tested details from practitioners who submit, chase and price out-of-network claims every week.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 486.32 Tm (Items: Give payers the NPI first, not just the EIN: Baker says insurers never locate an out-of-network provider by tax) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.10 Tm (ID but find the NPI immediately, and a dropped NPI is the usual reason a claim stalls [Dr. Lauren Baker -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.87 Tm (zsaby8gJNmg @ 00:13:48]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 440.65 Tm (In Murray's experience, an adjustment disorder on its own does not get reimbursed out-of-network, so a secondary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 425.42 Tm (diagnosis is needed. A payer asking for a W-9 on a first out-of-network claim is routine admin, not a trap [Alicia) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.20 Tm (Murray | The Therapist HQ ? - eXrZnEwRRH4 @ 00:26:08]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.97 Tm (Plans can cap member submission windows at as little as ninety days, so issue superbills monthly or have the software) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 379.75 Tm (send them automatically rather than letting clients hoard six months of paperwork [Craft Your Practice -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 364.52 Tm (tkUfu8WA56U @ 00:09:32]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.30 Tm (Before dropping a contract, check what that payer actually pays out-of-network: a Carter coaching client collects about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.07 Tm ($220 a visit billing full charges, against a self-pay rate of about $179 [Jarod Carter - cA7tBJf4KyY @ 00:05:52]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.85 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.62 Tm (The first split is who files. Jarod Carter calls the superbill handoff the lowest administrative burden path and runs a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.40 Tm (cash practice that way, but Carter also teaches that some payers in some regions make out-of-network billing far more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.17 Tm (lucrative: one coaching client with a roughly $179 self-pay rate sends the full undiscounted bill and collects about $220) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.95 Tm (a visit [cA7tBJf4KyY @ 00:02:21] [cA7tBJf4KyY @ 00:06:06]. Kym Tolson recommends the superbill route because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.72 Tm (it is easier on the provider, and when courtesy-filing in SimplePractice, Tolson marks accept assignment as no so the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.50 Tm (check goes to the client while the practice still collects the full self-pay rate [FpNL1YIlvD0 @ 00:02:42]. Alicia) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.27 Tm (Murray runs the opposite playbook across a fully out-of-network virtual group practice: complimentary billing, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.05 Tm (Murray credits for visible gains in retention and conversion over superbills alone, at the cost of storing insurance cards,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.82 Tm (driver's licenses and policyholder birth dates, and eventually hiring a biller once claim volume exceeded what Murray) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 152.60 Tm (could personally handle [eXrZnEwRRH4 @ 00:04:40] [eXrZnEwRRH4 @ 00:11:48]. The operator call is money) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 137.37 Tm (versus admin: Carter's test is whether you already have a billing department, and Murray's is whether your bandwidth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 122.15 Tm (can absorb rework.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.92 Tm (The sharpest disagreement is whether the practice should quote benefits at all. Jarod Carter uses Reimbursify to pull) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 91.70 Tm (out-of-network benefits quickly, yet tells superbill-only practices not to look them up for patients, because insurers) Tj ET
