BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (On the front end, the mechanics come down to timing and collecting cash at the point of service. MedConsults teaches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (a sequence: verify insurance right after scheduling, obtain pre-certification, counsel the patient, re-verify at the time of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (service, and collect co-pays on the spot. The reason it gives is that 'money collected now never becomes a receivable') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm ([YlcvgGZT9eQ @ 00:04:18]. Contempo Coding's Victoria runs verification the night before or days ahead to catch) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (terminated coverage and wrong payer order. She notes that Medicaid is usually the last payer and does not like to pay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (anything before everyone else does [pG2R1NwUlro @ 00:05:00]. As a supervisor, Victoria also trained front-desk staff) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (on incident-to and advanced-practitioner billing. Billing under the provider can earn 100% of the fee schedule, while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (many payers reduce pay on visits handled only by an APP. The AMA team adds a hard fix drawn from Chen's own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (loss. After a centralized business office relied on a 'payer matrix' instead of obtaining real prior auth, denied claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (were charged off silently. The fix is a communication workflow between the front desk and prior-auth/referral staff,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (plus a triage list of upcoming appointments [Ie5ARcGEY1g @ 00:06:52]. Etactics folds financial counseling and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (pre-visit estimates into the same layer, saying they cut the number of bills sent to collections [M-Mz0m1tdrQ @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (00:03:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Mid-cycle and claim submission run on scrubbers, clearinghouses, and speed. Samson describes claims going out as an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (837 EDI transmission through scrubber edits and clearinghouse logic. Analysts then read the 835 remittance to find the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (root cause and 'legally force' payment [RddJn-tA3OM @ 00:01:25]. The AMA defines a clean claim as 'one with all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (the information on it, free of errors and nothing missing.' It tells practices to set required-field edits for each payer with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (their vendor and fix every error before batch submission. The common gaps it lists are unchecked boxes, missing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (prior-auth numbers, and missing taxonomy or NPI. It also requires every CPT code to link to a diagnosis code, with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (code changes made without clinician approval [Ie5ARcGEY1g @ 00:19:04]. Amazing Charts' Greg layers a second) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (clearinghouse scrub on top of the PM scrub and works first-pass rejections within about an hour. His target is claims at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (carriers within 24 to 48 hours of receipt. An HL7 feed sweeps chart data on a set interval, so nobody pushes charges) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (manually at day-end [eKRUeJa5ZzQ @ 00:21:14]. RCM Mastery's adjudication split shows why the scrub matters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (About 65% of claims are paid in full, a quarter are paid only partially, and 'a solid 10% are just denied.' It calls claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (scrubbing an automated final check that massively boosts first-try payment [okx8geMd-gU @ 00:03:32].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (The back end is a disciplined sequence, and Inlera University gives the most granular playbook. Post payments using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (the EFT or bank-deposit date, not whenever is convenient. Reconcile with the bookkeeper, request deposit-only bank) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (access, and run everything through one revenue account. Work denials to zero, push unclear denials to the top of that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (payer's AR list, and leave 'breadcrumbs' in the account notes. For AR, pivot by payer and work the highest volume first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (Exclude claims under three weeks old, because payers pay in 7 to 14 days. Scan for odd amounts or codes before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (calling, and never work AR before posting is caught up [RvLjKE1S1eU @ 00:06:32]. MedConsults sets the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (productivity bar: 'Work 40 to 60 accounts a day and document every effort in the system notes' [YlcvgGZT9eQ @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (00:10:20]. On triage, PayerWatch's Ryan O'Hara rejects working denials in reverse gross-charge order. He preaches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm ('smart work': fight what you can win, even if that means writing off a $200,000 account you cannot win [cePrn8Rhav8) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (@ 00:12:00]. Amazing Charts takes the opposite line on small balances. Greg says they absolutely will chase a $10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (claim, and they status every claim in the 60-plus day bucket by phone or payer portal, all documented [eKRUeJa5ZzQ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.90 Tm (@ 00:33:11]. That split between selective and exhaustive AR work shapes staffing math.) Tj ET
