BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (bPFE9F4Y_Y4 @ 00:08:25]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (Start with the raw file, because EMS Healthcare Informatics insists anyone can open it. An 835 is a plain, unencrypted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (text file with no mandatory naming convention, so a .txt or .dat opens in Notepad or WordPad, but never edit it in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (Word-style editor because its formatting breaks a file that must stay pure [JfPjIRaIz-o @ 00:01:53]. It arrives as one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (continuous string, built from hierarchical loops, segments of related fields, and elements that hold the actual data, split) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (by delimiters: the asterisk is the most common element separator and the tilde the most common segment separator.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (The trick: in a text editor with global search-and-replace, key off the tilde and insert a carriage return so each segment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (lands on its own line [JfPjIRaIz-o @ 00:05:25]. The decoder is the implementation guide, the Bible bought from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (Washington Publishing and described as quite expensive. Walk the CLP line with it: CLP01 is your patient control) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (number, CLP02 status where 2 means processed as secondary, CLP03 total charge, CLP04 total paid, CLP05 patient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (responsibility, CLP06 filing indicator such as HM, and CLP07 the payer claim control number [JfPjIRaIz-o @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (00:07:45]. Michael Roberts, teaching as Professor Remit, adds that status 1 means processed as primary [HolIPG8-TV8) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (@ 00:00:55].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Michael Roberts then walks a full sample ERA top to bottom, promising you will know exactly where your money) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (went. ISA, GS and ST are the envelope you can mostly wave past; BPR is the payment line, here $1,250 sent by ACH) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (on November 5th; TRN is the check or EFT trace number used to match the deposit; N1 PR is the payer and N1 PE is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (the practice with its NPI [HolIPG8-TV8 @ 00:00:33]. The claim: CLP charges $200, pays $120, patient owes $20;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (SVC 99213 office visit; CAS CO45 for $60 written off and PR2 for $20 coinsurance; AMT B6 allowed of $140. His) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (balance check is $200 minus $60 equals $140 allowed, and $120 paid plus $20 patient equals $140 [HolIPG8-TV8 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (00:01:39]. Then the trap segment: PLB near the end pulls money from the whole payment, his sample being a $25) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (overpayment recovery, which is why a check can be smaller than its claims [HolIPG8-TV8 @ 00:02:04]. Jeremy Zug) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (describes the same hole from the posting floor: bill $100, the payer pays $80, the check says $70, and the missing $10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (is buried in a PLB recoupment for an error from three months ago, which on volume makes a huge difference) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm ([FE6Ns41GFH0 @ 00:08:18].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (Posting is where the decoding becomes cash control, and the speakers want proof before a dollar counts. InfiMed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (Health runs it as six software agents under an orchestrator: an 835 parser, ERA matching to claim and account, contract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (variance detection, patient balance allocation using the adjustment codes, bank deposit matching by trace number, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (exception routing, with two rules, posted means proven and people own write-offs, refunds and underpayment disputes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm ([uO7nW5fy5Y4 @ 00:01:25]. Health Weave RCM's manual version: match the deposit total to the remittance before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (closing the batch, post contractual, patient and payment amounts to separate buckets, check the math on every claim,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (and watch for provider-level recoupments [bPFE9F4Y_Y4 @ 00:09:19]. When a deposit lands with no ERA, Jeremy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (Zug's move is the payer portal, Availity, Optum or payer sites like Navanet, to download a PDF remittance and match it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (to the cash before posting, instead of 45 minutes of hold music; portals also take online corrections that process in days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (instead of 30 [FE6Ns41GFH0 @ 00:11:31]. For bulk triage, EMS's EDI Power Reader, a desktop application that) Tj ET
