BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.77 Tm (The costliest trap is the check that does not match its claims. Michael Roberts, speaking as Professor Remit, flags the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 366.55 Tm (PLB segment near the end of the 835 that takes money from the whole payment, using a $25 overpayment recovery,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.32 Tm (and warns it is easy to miss and is why a check can be smaller than its claims [HolIPG8-TV8 @ 00:02:04]. The Claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.10 Tm (Game X Practice Solutions puts numbers on the same leak: you billed $100, they paid 80, but the check was only $70,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.87 Tm (and the missing $10 is buried in a provider level adjustment, often a recoupment for an error from three months earlier,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 305.65 Tm (which is why autoposting cannot be set and forgotten [FE6Ns41GFH0 @ 00:08:18]. Health Weave RCM LLC adds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.42 Tm (that if you overlook these provider level adjustments, your deposit and your postings will never reconcile) Tj ET
